// Firebase Realtime Database stores JSON data in a JSON Tree structure

### Push new JSON data to the path
POST https://dmit2015-1252-oe01-swu-default-rtdb.asia-southeast1.firebasedatabase.app/Task.json
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "description": "Send Http Request",
  "priority": "High",
  "done": false
}

### Read JSON data by path
GET https://dmit2015-1252-oe01-swu-default-rtdb.asia-southeast1.firebasedatabase.app/Task.json

### Read JSON data by path and primary key value
@primaryKeyValue = -OkW4ZWMoaQXtWHc9bBy
GET https://dmit2015-1252-oe01-swu-default-rtdb.asia-southeast1.firebasedatabase.app/Task/{{primaryKeyValue}}.json

### Write JSON data - will replace all properties with the properties in the request body - if you miss a property it will be removed
PUT https://dmit2015-1252-oe01-swu-default-rtdb.asia-southeast1.firebasedatabase.app/Task/{{primaryKeyValue}}.json
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "description": "Start assignment 1",
  "priority": "High",
  "done": true
}

### Remove JSON data - use this if you want to delete data
@deletePrimaryKeyValue = -OkW4ZsAtUoKvByzHFL9
DELETE https://dmit2015-1252-oe01-swu-default-rtdb.asia-southeast1.firebasedatabase.app/Task/{{deletePrimaryKeyValue}}.json

### Update data - use this if you want to update some of the properties but not all of them
@patchPrimaryValue = -OkW4Z5_yyWm-nJrMO6q
PATCH https://dmit2015-1252-oe01-swu-default-rtdb.asia-southeast1.firebasedatabase.app/Task/{{primaryKeyValue}}.json
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "description": "Execute Http Request"
}